      <h1>What Is Bitcoin Hashrate?</h1>
      <p class="msc-learn-page__deck">Bitcoin hashrate is an estimate of how much proof-of-work computation is being applied to mining. Individual machines and pools can measure or estimate their own performance, but total network hashrate is not directly observable. It is inferred from accumulated chainwork and the time blocks took to arrive, so the result depends on the measurement window and natural block-time variance.</p>
      <ul class="msc-learn-page-meta"><li>Network</li><li>Shallow</li><li>Explainer</li><li>11 minutes</li><li>Reviewed 2026-07-18</li></ul>
